@startuml opponent-strategy-naive
' SPEC: _spec/apps/starchess/core/adjutant/naive/opponent-strategy.puml
' purpose: ADJUTANT (SCRIPT NAIVE) — deterministic plan search; commits only
' through addScAction. The shipped script behind /single and the tutorial.
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/adjutant.ts
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/context/**
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/strategies/**
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/ai/plans/**
' see also: ../cc-focus.puml (the omniscience contract, decided)
' see also: ../weight-ladder.puml (every naive weight and its tier)
' see also: _spec/packages/starchess-core/deploy-reach.puml (undefended)
' see also: ../strategic/strategic-economy.puml (shared Mecha gate, fog-gated twin)
!include ../../../../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title StarChess · Adjutant difficulty: ADJUTANT (SCRIPT NAIVE) — opponent strategy (plan)

package "App trigger" {
  component "BaseScreen / MatchStore\nautoQueueOpponent" as TRIG <<host>>
}

package "Strategy" {
  component "ai/adjutant.ts\norchestrator only" as AI <<app>>

  package "ai/context" {
    component "buildAdjutantCtx\nSCFEN → input variables" as CTX <<app>>
    component "vision · kingIntel · tactical\nmaterial · mines · pawns · geometry" as CTXP <<app>>
    component "posture\nexpand / seek / hunt → weights" as POST <<app>>
  }

  package "ai/strategies" {
    component "checks" as S1 <<app>>
    component "captures" as S2 <<app>>
    component "threats" as S3 <<app>>
    component "survival" as S4 <<app>>
    component "mapControl\n(+ promotion)" as S5 <<app>>
    component "economy\n(deploy mix)" as S6 <<app>>
  }

  package "ai/plans" {
    component "stacks\nB+C + C+F (charonForwardStacks)" as PL <<app>>
    component "simulate\nclearsCheck guard" as SIM <<app>>
  }
}

package "Reads" {
  component "board-queries\nvision · moves · mines · adjacent" as BQ <<db>>
  component "board/deploy-reach.ts\ndeployCovers — is it really undefended?" as DR <<db>>
  component "board/mine-contact.ts\nhostileMineOn — never step on a mine" as MC <<db>>
}

package "Command (same as human)" {
  component "addScAction\nqueue-action + validation" as Q <<async>>
}

package "Document" {
  database "ScFenSnapshot Q:" as SNAP <<db>>
}

TRIG ARROW_MAIN AI : snap in (opposite side)
AI ARROW_MAIN CTX : build once per turn
CTX ARROW_OPTIONAL CTXP : derive intel
CTX ARROW_OPTIONAL POST : resolve posture → weights
CTXP ARROW_OPTIONAL BQ : evaluate board
AI ARROW_MAIN S5 : generate + score\n(ctx read-only)
S5 -[hidden]- S1
AI ARROW_MAIN PL : compose B+C packages
AI ARROW_MAIN SIM : guard every plan
AI ARROW_MAIN Q : commit chosen plan
Q ARROW_MAIN SNAP : gated write
TRIG ARROW_OPTIONAL SNAP : APPLY_SNAPSHOT / store merge\n(one clock — no bypass reduce rules)

note bottom
  **Pattern:** Strategy → Command.
  **Turn shape:** context → posture weights → strategies
  (generate + score) → plans → guard → rank → commit.
  **Allowed:** adjutant → addScAction (same gates as human).
  **Forbidden:** adjutant → resolve-turn or raw Q: string edits.
  **Forbidden:** a second legality stack in the app for AI moves.
  **Forbidden:** a strategy that reads the snapshot directly, mutates
  the context, or branches on posture — weights are the only dial.
  **Forbidden:** importing from ""ai/strategic/**"" — this layer is below it.
  **Charon hunt (two-mode):** ""captures.ts"" proposes B insta-kills while
  ""enemyCanJump"" (enemy gasIncome < 3) is false, else F teleport-guesses at
  top-3 mirrored warp predictions (free-aim diagonal + strike verified);
  ""charonForwardStacks"" pairs each F with a classical that neither moves
  the mecha nor occupies/screens the aim. Strategic twin mirrors both modes.
end note

note as N_OMNI
  **The naive script is omniscient about the Command Center, on purpose.**
  ""ctx.enemyCC"" is ""findCC(map, enemy)"" and is never fog-filtered, so the
  per-type check bonuses (""SNEAK_HOVERBIKE_CHECK"" 2_000, ""MARINE_CHECK_CC"" 1_500,
  the Mecha ""diagonal"", ""TACTICAL_JUMP_CHECK_CC"" 2_000) aim at the real square
  whether or not the script can see it. That is the decided contract, not a
  defect: this is the weaker difficulty, and the fog-honest treatment belongs
  to the strategic script.

  **Two terms are still fog-gated:** ""attackCC"" and ""chaseCC"" test
  ""vision.enemyCCVisible"" explicitly. The gate is close to redundant —
  ""resolvePosture"" only returns ""hunt"" when the CC is visible, and those are
  the only postures where either weight is non-zero — but it is cheap and it
  documents which two terms were meant to depend on sight. Full split in
  ""../cc-focus.puml"".
end note

note as N_UNDEFENDED
  **"Undefended" now means undefended against a deploy too.** ""captures.ts""
  asks ""deployCovers"" on the **POST-move** board, for the enemy side, with
  ""snap.gasIncome[enemy]"" and ""ctx.storedFor(enemy)"": a Marine the enemy can
  recapture by dropping a unit off its Command Center is not free, so
  ""HUNT_UNDEFENDED_MARINE"" stays off.

  That predicate used to be a private, Marine-only ""canGasDeployDefend"" that
  imported from ""ai/strategic/context"" — the one place this layer reached
  upward. It now lives in ""board/deploy-reach.ts"", below both layers, and the
  only strategic field naive reads is the optional ""ctx.winning"", which the
  naive build simply leaves absent.
end note

AI .. N_OMNI
S2 .. N_UNDEFENDED
S2 ARROW_OPTIONAL DR : deployCovers (POST-move, enemy)
S4 ARROW_OPTIONAL MC : never jump onto a mine
S5 ARROW_OPTIONAL MC : never drop / step onto a mine

note as N_BISHOP_CAPS
  Same-color bishops share diagonals, so the
  helper caps Mecha at four total and two per
  square color (a1 dark parity). Total four is
  absolute while per-color two still admits a
  big-threat capture, crush-replace nets out first.
end note

note as N_BISHOP_TAKE
  Per-color two admits only a big-threat take where
  fresh bishop crushes queen or rook on square or
  captures one classically. Knight, bishop, pawn
  takes never qualify; Charon fails since fresh
  deploy spent special, always-visible, ladder kept.
end note

S6 .. N_BISHOP_CAPS
S6 .. N_BISHOP_TAKE
@enduml
